Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:00:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(entities): send saddles and tame state for Bedrock mounts

Bedrock reports a mount's saddle with the SADDLED actor flag and a
tamed horse with TAMED. Java keeps the saddle in the SADDLE equipment
slot and the tame state in AbstractHorse's flags byte, and neither was
translated. A saddled horse therefore looked unsaddled to the Java
client: it drew no saddle and no jump bar, although native Bedrock's
HUD has a horse_jump_renderer inside the experience bar.

Abstract horses now get Java's tame (0x02), eating (0x10) and standing
(0x20) bits from TAMED, EATING and STANDING. Saddleable mounts (horses,
donkeys, mules, skeleton and zombie horses, camels, pigs, striders and
nautili, but not llamas) get a SADDLE equipment update whenever the
SADDLED flag changes.

A jumpable saddled mount makes the Java client send PLAYER_COMMAND
START_RIDING_JUMP and STOP_RIDING_JUMP, which previously disconnected
with "Unhandled PlayerCommandAction". A Bedrock 1.26.60.5 client riding
a tamed, saddled horse on a local BDS sent no player action for a
charged jump: only JumpPressedRaw, JumpDown, Jumping and WantUp while
held, then JumpReleasedRaw, in a client-predicted vehicle. The Java
input path already sends the same sequence, so both commands are
accepted without sending anything.

